  "58": {
    "inputs": {
      "prompts": "A tiny, anthropomorphic hedgehog wearing a miniature baker's hat is carefully decorating a large, multi-tiered birthday cake in a cozy, sun-drenched cottage kitchen. He stands on his tiptoes, his small paws gently placing a single, glowing, golden sprinkle on the top tier, a look of intense concentration on his face. The kitchen is warm and cluttered with mixing bowls, a sack of flour, and a copper kettle. A soft, diffused sunlight streams through a leaded glass window, casting long, warm shadows across the wooden floor. The camera is a medium shot, slightly low-angled to emphasize the cake's height, and holds steady. A small bluebird chirps from the windowsill.\n---\nThe hedgehog steps back, admiring his work with a proud, wide-eyed expression, a single tear of joy welling in his eye. Suddenly, he loses his balance on a stray drop of batter, his arms flailing as he stumbles backward onto the soft, flour-dusted floor with a quiet puff of white dust. The bluebird lets out a sharp, startled chirp. The camera quickly pans down to capture his fall, moving from a medium shot to a close-up of his surprised face as he lands. The lighting remains warm, but the cloud of flour momentarily catches the sunlight, creating a sparkling effect in the air around him.\n---\nStruggling back to his feet, the little baker is shocked to see a large, clumsy paw reaching from off-screen and swiping the entire top tier of the cake. A towering, but equally tiny, moose chef in a stained apron is revealed, his mouth full of frosting as he tries to look innocent. The hedgehog shakes his head in dismay, his ears drooping. The camera is a medium two-shot, capturing the moment from the moose's back as he leans over the table, then cutting to a close-up of the hedgehog’s horrified reaction. The lighting shifts slightly, becoming a little more dramatic with a shadow falling over the hedgehog’s face.\n---\nThe moose, realizing his mistake, offers a sheepish smile and a small, velvet bag of magical ingredients as an apology, his massive hooves surprisingly gentle. The hedgehog's expression softens from anger to curiosity as he peers into the bag, a single shimmering star-dust mote floating out. He takes a hesitant step forward, gesturing for the moose to help him. The camera slowly zooms in from a wide shot of the kitchen to a tight over-the-shoulder shot of the hedgehog looking into the bag, the light from the dust illuminating his face. The background fades into a warm, magical blur.\n---\nThe hedgehog and the moose are now working side-by-side, the hedgehog directing the moose as the latter carefully places a new golden star on the repaired cake's top. They look at each other and share a triumphant smile, a true friendship born from the mishap. The bluebird flies down and lands on the moose's antler. The camera pulls back and upwards in a slow, gentle crane shot, revealing the entire scene in the warm kitchen, the perfect cake at the center. The natural light from the window flares softly, creating a heartwarming, wholesome glow over the two friends.",
      "max_length": 512,
      "clip": [
        "47",
        0
      ]
    },
